{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And Elohim said: Let there be light.</b> In this section the word אוֹר (light) is written five times, and on the fourth day the word מָאוֹר (luminary) is written five times with the addition of the letter מ״ם, and there is a wondrous intention in this. For we find that the Sages said (Chagigah 12a): the light that was created on the first day was hidden away; and there is the opinion of the one who says: they are the very same luminaries that were created on the first day and were not suspended until the fourth day. And these two midrashim appear to contradict each other. But the truth is not so, for everyone agrees that the light of the first day was a great light and was hidden away; and these luminaries that were suspended on the fourth day are not the essence of the light itself, but rather they received their light from the spark of the supernal light that was created on the first day. Therefore, regarding it, Scripture uses the expression אוֹר, because it was the essence of the light; but regarding the luminaries of the fourth day, it uses for each one the expression מָאוֹר with the addition of the מ״ם, to indicate that they received their light from another light greater than themselves, as the מ״ם indicates. And according to this the midrashim do not contradict each other, for the first light was hidden away for the righteous according to everyone, and the luminaries of the fourth day received a spark of the first light — and if so, they are certainly the very same luminaries, for the part is included within the whole. And through this it is also settled how that which was created could also have been hidden away — and this is a precious interpretation."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T23:32:22.253022969Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}